nodecode-github-app is a rewrite of himanusia's himanusia/hermes-github-app-plugin:

  https://github.com/himanusia/hermes-github-app-plugin
  commit 2adfd020f93a5d71a563e94c88738fb8e64335f8
  author himanusia (https://github.com/himanusia)
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 himanusia (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's seven tools and the identity behind them, as one cell.
The verbs, their arguments and their answers are the original's (github_app/tools.py,
TOOL_SPECS): github_identity, github_create_issue, github_comment_issue,
github_list_issues, github_get_issue, github_review_pr and github_merge_pr, with
the same owner/name repository rule, the same positive-number and full-40-character
SHA checks, the same compact JSON answers, and the attribution (auth method and
actor) on every result. So is the credential order (github_app/client.py,
_resolve_credentials): a GitHub App's App ID, installation ID and private key
sign an RS256 JWT, the JWT is exchanged for an installation token, and the actor
is the App's own <slug>[bot]; failing that a GITHUB_TOKEN/GH_TOKEN, failing that
an already-signed-in gh CLI. The original delegated RSA signing to PyJWT; here
ironclad signs the same PKCS#1 v1.5 SHA-256 block, and the PEM (PKCS#1 or
PKCS#8) is read by a small DER reader, so the cell needs no Python and no
openssl. The write gate is the original's own allow_write_actions setting, and
its stale-head rules are kept: a review refuses unless commit_id is the live
head, and a merge always carries the head SHA it expects.

Left out: the pre_tool_call approval hook, which built a rule key from a fresh
UUID so an "always" answer never persisted and blocked any write payload over
3000 characters. A cell has no approval prompt of its own, so the original's
allow_write_actions setting is the whole gate and the two head-SHA arguments are
the second check; the payload-size block goes with the prompt. Also left out:
the Hermes profile .env fallback and the secret_scope read (a cell reads its own
section of the config, so unrelated profile secrets are never touched), the
thread-local client bookkeeping that closed a client after each call, the /app
slug lookup when app_slug is set, the GH_CONFIG_DIR routed-profile check in the
gh CLI fallback, and the redirect-refusing urllib opener (NLK:HTTP follows up to
five redirects; the token rides only the https API base the section names, which
is validated the way the original validated it). The original's Hermes-side
toolset name and its check_fn gate are the cell's registration and start refusal.
